Stream function wave case in a one wavelength domain with periodic boundaries.

A progressive stream function wave (H = 0.125 m, T = 2 s, depth 0.4 m, wavelength
3.787 m) is propagated for 15 periods with interFoam, interIsoFoam and interIsoGoam
(geometric gravity model) on four meshes (nx x nz = 95x20 ... 760x160). Case 0036 of
each scan runs streamFunFoam, which evaluates the exact solution, as the reference.

Scans
-----

gravityModelScanParms.csv          -> gravityModelScan: adaptive time step,
                                      maxCo 0.5, 0.2, 0.1, 0.05 on each mesh
gravityModelScanParms_fixedDt.csv  -> gravityModelScan_fixedDt: fixed time step,
                                      dt0, dt0/2, dt0/4, dt0/8 with dt0 = 0.02 s
                                      on 95x20, halved with each mesh refinement

Requirements
------------

Stream function wave solution (streamFunFoam):
https://github.com/InterFlowers/streamFunctionWave

Running scans with parmScanner:
https://github.com/isoAdvector/cfdTools

Post-processing: python3 with numpy, scipy and matplotlib; pvbatch (ParaView) for the
case illustration.

Reproducing the paper figures
-----------------------------

./Allrun                    runs (or completes) both scans and post-processes them
./Allrun -postProcessOnly   only post-processes existing scans
./Allclean [-scans]         removes the generated files (and with -scans the scans)

A single scan can also be run by hand after sourcing cfdTools:

parmScanner -file gravityModelScanParms.csv -exec Allrun -parallel

Scripts
-------

analyseScan.py            accuracy and efficiency metrics per run (CSV): wave height
                          error from a quadratic trend through all waves, wave-to-wave
                          scatter, shape and phase errors, spurious velocities, cost
paperFigures.py           paper figures from the metrics and the case time series
paperData.py              numbers behind the paper in paperData/ (tracked in git):
                          copies of the metrics and the derived statistics
                          quoted in the text
renderCaseIllustration.py mesh and wave illustration (pvbatch, caseIllustration.pvsm)
plotCrestHeight.py        crest, trough and wave height against time for chosen cases;
                          shared functions for the other scripts
plotWaveHeightBySolver.py relative wave height, one panel per solver
plotWaveHeightByParameters.py  relative wave height, one panel per parameter set
exportSeries.py           time series excerpts as a JSON/JS file for web reports
compareResults.py         surface elevation and max velocity against time

